Queue Mechanism
Daily TV app collection updates routine: How to set up the display and collections 
system 
Queue mechanism 
The user can add 20 collections in a queue at any time. 
A certain amount of space is reserved on the TV to store one or of these collections
- lets say x gb. Our system calculates how many of the collections, 
starting from the first one, can be sent to the TV. (eg. if x is 2 gb, and
say col. 1 is 800 mb, collection 2. is 600 mb, collection 3 is 800 mb, 
then only the first 2 are sent.)
Once each of these collections have been displayed, then the TV app sends a 
note to the mobile app asking to send the next batch. If the mobile phone is not
 in the vicinity (communication failed), then it keeps on trying every 10 minutes. 
 This loop keeps on repeating.


